PullTest
├── when funding is non-empty AND route is empty
│ └── it reverts with {RouteFundingRequiresRoute}
├── given funding is non-empty AND route is non-empty
│ ├── when a funding token is currency0
│ │ └── it reverts with {InvalidFundingToken}
│ ├── when a funding token is currency1
│ │ └── it reverts with {InvalidFundingToken}
│ ├── when a funding token is native
│ │ └── it adds the amount to expectedValue
│ ├── when a funding token is ERC20 AND amount GT 0
│ │ └── it pulls the amount via Permit2 into the zap
│ └── when a funding token is ERC20 AND amount EQ 0
│     └── it pulls nothing and still grants the Permit2 allowance
├── given pool-token budget
│ ├── when currency0 is native
│ │ └── it adds amount0In to expectedValue
│ ├── when currency0 is ERC20 AND amount0In GT 0
│ │ └── it pulls amount0In via Permit2
│ ├── when currency0 is ERC20 AND amount0In EQ 0
│ │ └── it does not pull currency0
│ └── when amount1In GT 0
│     └── it pulls amount1In via Permit2
├── when msg.value != expectedValue
│ └── it reverts with {InvalidEthValue}
└── when address(this).balance LT expectedValue
    └── it reverts with {InvalidEthValue}
